[{"code":"view_changes_model","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":22,"col":8},"end":{"line":22,"col":19}},"title":"VIEW CHANGES THE MODEL","message":"`view` changes the record at `model` in place, but the runtime hands `view` the\nmodel to read only.\n\n22|main = Tea.sandbox { init = λ⊤ → { count = 0, label = \"a\" }, update = λ_ m → m, view = view }\n          ^^^^^^^^^^^ the runtime hands `view` the model here\n\nThe runtime keeps the model it hands `view` for the next message and the next\nrender, so a change in place would be seen by both.\n\nLet `view` build a new record instead, or change a copy made with `Record.copy`.\n\nThis is the platform's rule for `view`, whether or not anything else reads the\nrecord."}]
